open qualification failures, not ignored tests or a completed cutover seal.

S8C browser source-boundary correction, 2026-10-03
-------------------------------------------------

This correction starts from C `d0d1f4d2840cea6f559b5823b9fa987ed0cb1122`,
on R15 `54a0397e126a3b21616b8ccad728d293d884c96e`, with R26 `3f1f23772a`
and R06 `e5101287f1` below it. The newer stack identities include the R26
selector regression but do not replace C's preceding fixes. Historical suite
results above are retained as history, not attributed to this correction.

The four current review obligations are closed at their shared owners:

1. Static sources retain their defining nominal origin and transported package
   identity in the manifest. The bootstrap passes those values to the same
   provenance-aware source resolver used by served documents. The regression
   compares complete enum nominal and schema identities with native compilation,
   not just printed values. Old static nominal sources without provenance are
   refused with a regeneration instruction rather than assigned a new identity.

2. Publication invokes the selected package's actual WASM compiler and shared
   resident target preflight. `ProgramCompiler::preflight_resident_artifact`
   reuses the loader's effect-free provider planning facts and resident admission
   owner. It does not activate an instance, start drivers, run turns, or deliver
   effects. There is no duplicate scalar/operator feature checklist. Node.js 22+
   is an explicit publication dependency, and the relevant CI jobs install it.
   Native planning and target admission finish before any output is published.
   The admitted JS/WASM/snippet bytes and configuration text are frozen and those
   same bytes are published, including when the original inputs change during
   the probe. The child uses its stable package directory, bounded diagnostics
   and a 60-second admission deadline.

3. Every ordinary WasmProject construction path retains the same pointer handle
   installed in its input driver. Readiness reflects the running driver, not
   merely a configured host. Static bootstrap events deliver normalized position,
   primary-button state and elapsed time; stop, unload and error detach listeners.
   The existing WasmDocument lifecycle remains unchanged.

4. Rich comment parsing is bounded by the physical line. An incomplete opener
   rewinds speculative markup and consumes inert literal text without refunding
   work. LF, CRLF, bare CR, EOF, scalar chunk boundaries and exhausted processing
   fuel are covered; completed rich markup remains structured. Public bundle
   execution and rendered HTML preserve the following program and escape markup.

